Fix the lifetime of the vbc_turning class names.

class_create() stores the name pointer it is given, and on 6.18
dev_uevent_name() returns dev->class->name for every uevent on a class
device.  vbc_turning_ndp_init() passes a stack buffer, so once it returns
the class name points into the freed kernel stack of the modprobe task:
the first udevtrigger write to /sys/devices/virtual/vbc_turning0/.../uevent
faults in add_uevent_var() -> vsnprintf() -> string() and panics the kernel
(observed 2026-10-28 on the OpenWrt boot, 20 s in, from procd's
/sbin/udevtrigger).

Keep one name buffer per turning device for the life of the module.

--- a/sound/soc/sprd/unisoc/dai/vbc_v4/vbc_dai/vbc-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sprd/unisoc/dai/vbc_v4/vbc_dai/vbc-dai.c
@@ -3487,7 +3487,11 @@
 	unsigned int minor = 0;
 	u8 index = 0;
-	char ndp_name[32];
+	/* class_create() keeps this pointer: dev_uevent_name() reads
+	 * dev->class->name on every uevent, so the buffer must outlive this
+	 * function and the modprobe task's kernel stack. */
+	static char ndp_names[AUD_TURNING_PRO_CNTS][32];
+	char *ndp_name;
 
 	result = alloc_chrdev_region(&devid, AUD_TURNING_MINOR_START, AUD_TURNING_PRO_CNTS, AUDIO_TURNING_PATH_BASE);
 	if (result < 0) {
@@ -3513,9 +3517,10 @@
-		memset(&ndp_name[0], 0, sizeof(char) * 32);
-		sprintf(&ndp_name[0], "%s%d", AUDIO_TURNING_PATH_BASE, index);
+		ndp_name = ndp_names[index];
+		memset(ndp_name, 0, sizeof(ndp_names[index]));
+		snprintf(ndp_name, sizeof(ndp_names[index]), "%s%d", AUDIO_TURNING_PATH_BASE, index);
 		pr_info("%s,ndp_name = %s !\n", __func__, ndp_name);
 		aud_turning[index].turing_class = class_create(ndp_name);
 		if (IS_ERR(aud_turning[index].turing_class)) {
